## Problem 3: Array Reversal (In-Place)

**Question:**
Reverse the elements of a character array `char[] letters` in-place (without creating a second array).

**Solution:**
*Logic: Use two pointers, one at the start and one at the end, swapping elements and moving inward until they meet.*

```java
public static void reverseArray(char[] letters) {
    int start = 0;
    int end = letters.length - 1;

    while (start < end) {
        // Swap elements
        char temp = letters[start];
        letters[start] = letters[end];
        letters[end] = temp;

        // Move pointers inward
        start++;
        end--;
    }
}
```

